<title>UK: UK liquidation fees for BCCI top $200 million.</title>
<headline>UK liquidation fees for BCCI top $200 million.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fees paid to Deloitte and Touche, the liquidator in Britain of BCCI, totalled $203.6 million in the period to January 15, the date on which its last annual report was drawn up, the government said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Junior trade and industry minister John Taylor said in a written parliamentary answer that expenses to that date totalled an additional $6 million.</p>
<p>BCCI's international operations were shut down in July 1991 after allegations of huge fraud.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
</text>
